WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.180
There's something that might seem confusing
about Iran.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.610
The country has an unelected Supreme Leader
at the top, but it also has a president who's

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.920
democratically elected in votes that are far
from perfect, but sure look pretty important.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.240
So is Iran a dictatorship or is it a democracy?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.939
As it turns out, it's both, and seeing that
goes a long way to explaining why the country

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:25.400
is the way it is.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:31.400
Iran as we know it today began with a revolution
in 1979, which culminated in a simple referendum

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.820
that March: Islamic Republic, Yes or No?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.790
But what is an Islamic Republic?

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.950
How can a country's government be both theocratic
and representative?

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.600
Iran's revolutionary leaders didn't really know the answer either, and they never agreed.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.570
So they ended up creating a government that has these two systems mashed together.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:54.850
Some parts are elected, some are unelected,
and they're all tangled together in this kind of mess..

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:58.240
There's a real tension between those two systems.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.250
Iranians elect (more or less democratically)
the president, the parliament, which is

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.710
called the majles,  and a really important
body called the Assembly of Experts.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.429
We'll get to that later.

00:01:08.429 --> 00:01:14.179
At the same time there's the unelected theocracy:
the Supreme Leader, the judiciary, the military,

00:01:14.179 --> 00:01:15.130
and others.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.530
Still, the Supreme Leader really does dominate
Iran.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:23.170
He sets the tone for the country's politics
and policies, including its nuclear program

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.270
and its official hostility to the West.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.749
But what happens when the Supreme Leader dies
or gets sick?

00:01:28.749 --> 00:01:31.569
This turns out to be a really important question.

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:36.999
The Supreme Leader is picked by a group of
about 90 senior Iranian political and clerical

00:01:36.999 --> 00:01:39.509
leaders that's called the Assembly of Experts.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:45.100
But here's where Iran's Islamic Republic system
gets important: the Assembly's members are

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.429
elected in a national vote.

00:01:47.429 --> 00:01:53.939
This year, on February 26, Iranians will elect
an entirely new Assembly of Experts for an

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:55.149
8-year term.

00:01:55.149 --> 00:02:00.200
Even Ali Khamenei, the current Supreme Leader,
has acknowledged that he's like to die in

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:00.999
that time.

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:05.929
Iranian politics are really split right now,
with moderates rapidly rising after the nuclear

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:08.410
deal helped open the economy.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.140
If they do well in February's election, then
when Khamenei dies, they might pick a new

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.280
Supreme Leader who shares their views.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.629
That could change Iran as we know it for a
generation.

00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:24.510
This all goes to show that we think of Iran
as just another dictatorship, and indeed it

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.470
does have a dictator at the top, but it's
also a democracy.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:32.560
It's got loud political disagreements and
vigorous debates over its future.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.010
This election in February is a rare moment,
once in a generation, when Iran's democratic

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.349
elements become more powerful than its theocratic
elements.

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:47.430
Iranians have an opening here to try to transform
their country. If the take it, and if they're

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.799
successful, Iran could look very different
in for quite awhile.

